@independence_2025
# prose-audit: Grade B — Mentzen, Braun, PiS, Warsaw organisers and threatened minorities now contest a street with institutional memory, and every mobilisation strategy has an authored owner and cost.
title: The 2025 Independence Day March
subtitle: Mentzen, Braun and PiS compete for the street
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 34
order: 20
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/poland/cards/national-left-rally.webp
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 11
on-arrival: last_independence_march_year = 2025; far_right_street_capacity += 4; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -5; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 6; public_mood_pending_national_security_salience += 5

= November 2025 — Three rivals on the right

**Sławomir Mentzen's** Konfederacja, **Grzegorz Braun's** Crown movement and
PiS all arrive in Warsaw wanting to own the same national symbols. Their
competition does not make the street safer: nationalist organisers can push
one another toward the slogan or confrontation most likely to dominate the
broadcast.

Lewica is no longer improvising its first response. Civic organisers remember
the alternative celebrations we built; anti-fascists remember our counter-
marches; lawyers, police and minority groups remember whether monitoring kept
people safe. A social-patriotic current also wants to enter the main march and
deny the right exclusive ownership of the flag. Whichever line we repeat will
inherit trained people—and promises they expect us to keep.

- @ind25_civic
- @ind25_join
- @ind25_security
- @ind25_counter

@ind25_civic
title: Expand the civic-independence alternative
subtitle: [? if civic_independence_investment >= 3: The permanent network now funds the march itself. No resource cost.?][? if civic_independence_investment < 3: Cost: 1 resource.?]
choose-if: civic_independence_investment >= 3 or resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The annual operation cannot be staffed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1 if civic_independence_investment < 3; civic_independence_investment += 1 if civic_independence_investment < 3; independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition"; civic_independence_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 6; local_network += 2; public_trust += 2; far_right_street_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "A permanent civic tradition contests the radical-right monopoly"

Municipal stages, veterans, unions and cultural organisations offer a national
celebration that neither hides the flag nor asks families to walk through a
radical-right column. Another year of the same route turns an alternative event
into a tradition with its own volunteers, audience and public expectation.

- @poland_event_queue: File the civic Independence Day

@ind25_join
title: March as the social-patriotic Left and force the right to share its stage
subtitle: The caucus grows while Mentzen, Braun and nationalist organisers contest its presence.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March"; independence_join_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 5; social_patriot_support += 10; left_cultural_position += 4; left_right_score += 4; rural_support += 2; progressives_dissent += 9; spring_dissent += 7; razem_dissent += 6; minority_safety -= 2; far_right_street_capacity += 2; far_right_fragmentation += 4; news_headline = "A social-patriotic Left column turns the march into a fight over ownership"

The social-patriotic Left enters behind its own unions, welfare slogans and
red-and-white banners. Mentzen's stewards, Braun's supporters and nationalist
organisers each contest its presence, proving the march has more than one
owner. Rural and conservative-left supporters notice; progressive and minority
organisers ask why the party made them share a security perimeter with the far right.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the Left column inside the march

@ind25_security
title: Apply a neutral security plan and deny every camp a martyr
subtitle: Publish one assembly standard for police, organisers and people who may need protection.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring"; independence_monitor_years += 1; police_trust += 4 if left_in_government = 1; media_capacity += 2 if left_in_government = 0; minority_safety += 3; constitutional_restraint += 3; braun_martyrdom -= 1; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 4; public_mood_pending_national_security_salience += 6; news_headline = "The march receives a published assembly standard and monitoring record"

A published assembly standard governs routes, police intervention and evidence
for every camp. [? if left_in_government: The security services know the
government will defend proportionate enforcement rather than demand a partisan
show.?][? if not left_in_government: Lewica's legal monitors publish the record
the government and organisers will later have to answer.?] Braun receives less
martyr footage; threatened communities receive clearer routes to help.

- @poland_event_queue: File the monitored march

@ind25_counter
title: Mobilise the largest anti-fascist counter-march yet
subtitle: Put a visible force beside threatened communities and give the right the confrontation frame.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation"; independence_counter_years += 1; organiser_energy -= 3; progressive_credibility += 5; minority_safety += 3; far_right_street_capacity += 3; braun_martyrdom += 2; news_headline = "Competing marches turn Warsaw into the month's whole political frame"

Anti-fascist groups, unions and minority organisations fill a second route
through Warsaw. People threatened by the main march see a force prepared to
stand with them. The right answers with its own mobilisation, Braun gains the
confrontation frame, and every other meaning of Independence Day disappears
behind two crowds and the police line between them.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the counter-march

@matysiak_razem_2025
# prose-audit: Grade A — The confrontation is staged through a certified delegate roll, rival programme speeches and a two-chair vote; the three choices identify who controls Razem and who must register a successor.
title: Razem decides Paulina Matysiak's future
subtitle: Leadership challenge, Zandberg split or expulsion
face-image: img/poland/events/adrian-zandberg-2020.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 25
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and matysiak_resolution_done = 0 and ((month = 11 and matysiak_party = "Razem") or (social_patriot_active = 1 and month >= 9 and month <= 11 and (matysiak_party = "Razem" or matysiak_party = "Lewica Patriotyczna")))
on-arrival: {!
const socialPatriotBoost = Q.social_patriot_active
    ? 8 + Math.min(8, (Number(Q.social_patriot_strength) || 0) * 0.20)
    : 0;
Q.matysiak_development_score = Math.round(
    24 + (Number(Q.matysiak_development_pressure) || 0) +
    socialPatriotBoost +
    Math.max(
        -10,
        Math.min(
            16,
            ((Number(Q.economic_issue_salience) || 40) -
                (Number(Q.cultural_issue_salience) || 30)) * 0.30
        )
    ) +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_right_score) || 30) - 30) * 0.35 +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_poll) || 10) - 12) * 0.7 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) * 0.08
);
Q.news_headline = "Razem votes on Matysiak's developmental challenge";
!}

= November 2025 — Who gets to define Razem?

Razem's national council publishes the delegate roll and asks both statutory
chairs to certify it. **Adrian Zandberg** defends a democratic-socialist party
built around housing, public ownership and organised labour. **Paulina
Matysiak** answers with rail, nuclear power, regional investment and economic
sovereignty. Her programme turns Razem rightward on culture without making it
economically liberal.

[? if social_patriot_active: Lewica Patriotyczna's organisers give Matysiak an
additional caucus beyond her original Razem network.?] If her development
campaign has secured enough delegates, she can take the first chair or force
Zandberg's current to leave. If it has not, Zandberg's majority can expel her
and convert the dispute into a separate developmental party. The second chair
remains a statutory office whichever programme wins.

- @matysiak_leadership
- @matysiak_own_party
- @matysiak_expulsion

